  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member installing SwiftHFR, I want the app to show the HFR+ icon on the Home Screen, in its light, dark, clear and tinted appearances, as the legacy app does. The current target ships **no icon**: `App/SwiftHFR/Assets.xcassets/AppIcon.appiconset/Contents.json` declares a 1024 slot with no image. Milestone M4 (parity, App Store blocker). Operator request, 2026-11-07.\n\n### Legacy (read-only, @ 2440d79)\n- **Main icon**: an Icon Composer layered icon, `SuperHFRplus/Assets/Icon-RedFace3D.icon/`. It holds `icon.json` and `Assets/redface-background.png`, `redface-eyel.png`, `redface-eyer.png`, …, with per-appearance opacity specializations.\n  - Wired in `SuperHFRplus.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj:757, 1803, 3627, 4833` as `folder.iconcomposer.icon` in Resources.\n  - Selected with `ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME = \"Icon-RedFace3D\"` at `:6040, :6125`.\n- **Second layered icon**: `SuperHFRplus/Assets/AlternativeIcons/Icon-RedFace3DBig.icon/`.\n- **Alternates** (LOT-123 scope, not this issue): `HFRswift/Swift/Assets.xcassets/{Beta,Blue,Classic,Classic-Blue,Classic-Red,White}.appiconset`, plus the `setAlternateIconName` options in `AppSettingsView.swift:40-80, 216`: Classique Yellow / Red, Défaut, REDFACE, REDFACE Blue, Beta, Blue, White.\n\n### Scope\n1. Copy `Icon-RedFace3D.icon` (the whole folder, unchanged art) into the app target. Make it the app icon:\n   - `ASSETCATALOG_COMPILER_APPICON_NAME`, following ADR 0012 for project-file changes (the folder-synchronized group, or the minimal reviewed `project.pbxproj` change);\n   - keep or remove the empty `AppIcon.appiconset` so that only one icon source is active;\n   - Xcode 27 builds the light, dark, clear and tinted renditions from the `.icon` file.\n2. Copy `Icon-RedFace3DBig.icon` next to it, not wired. LOT-123 uses it as an alternate.\n3. Credit the art in CREDITS.md: it comes from the legacy app (PolyForm-NC; the legacy authors).\n4. Add a GAP row: main icon ported unchanged.\n5. **Out of scope**: the 8 alternate icons and the picker (LOT-123, #214), and new art.\n\n### Acceptance\n- CI \"App build + tests\" is green, and the built `.app` contains the compiled icon (`Assets.car`, `CFBundleIcons`). Check with `xcrun assetutil --info` or `plutil` in CI logs if available; otherwise it is a Mac check.\n- Mac check: Home Screen in light, dark, clear and tinted; Settings › Display icon size; Spotlight.\n\n### Routing\nSonnet 5.5 writes, Opus 5.5 reviews. The art is ported unchanged, so this is mechanical asset and build-setting work (AGENTS.md §6). Claimed for the cloud child `ext/francoisgn-icon`.",
